        "id": 1395690
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-01T09:27:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The configuration for Jaina is as follows: \n```\nCONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_USB_PD_MAX_VOLTAGE_MV\u003d20000\nCONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_USB_PD_MAX_CURRENT_MA\u003d3000\nCONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_USB_PD_MAX_POWER_MW\u003d45000\n```\nSince we support up to 20V, the system must be able to switch power profiles when a 45W adapter (20V/2.25A) is plugged in.",
      "parentUuid": "0e57581d_df71bc95",
      "revId": "a49d935432923085d1d4bfbbd74dd0c7530a0cd0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2fbb67d5_194152d4",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1141739
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-01T10:02:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, 20V is supported. But if the adapter offers both 20V/2.25A and 15V/3A, the EC defaults to 15V to optimize performance. This is by design.\n\nIf the adapter only provides a single 45W profile (20V/2.25A), the EC will use it.",
      "parentUuid": "f0f35fd4_eb1d7ff2",
      "revId": "a49d935432923085d1d4bfbbd74dd0c7530a0cd0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fc86a416_f146b0e8",
